# Reverse Proxy Configuration

1. Understand the purpose of a reverse proxy
2. Identify where to apply force HTTPS in the network architecture (e.g., in front of your app servers)
3. Configure TLS termination by setting up a reverse proxy like nginx, Caddy, or Cloudflare
4. Set routing rules for different API paths and requests using the configured proxy
5. Implement load balancing strategies if needed
6. Hide internal server details from clients behind the proxy
